      "source": "Thompson AJ et al. Lancet Neurol. 2018;17(2):162-173",
      "summary": "Revised diagnostic criteria requiring demonstration of dissemination in space (DIS) and dissemination in time (DIT). DIS requires lesions in 2 or more of 4 characteristic CNS areas: periventricular, cortical/juxtacortical, infratentorial, and spinal cord. DIT can be demonstrated by simultaneous enhancing and non-enhancing lesions, or new T2/enhancing lesion on follow-up MRI, or CSF oligoclonal bands."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The 2017 McDonald criteria allow MS diagnosis with: (1) 2 or more clinical attacks with objective evidence of 2 lesions; (2) 2 attacks with 1 objective lesion plus DIS criteria; (3) 1 attack with objective evidence of 2 lesions plus DIT criteria; or (4) 1 attack with 1 objective lesion plus both DIS and DIT criteria. Importantly, CSF oligoclonal bands can substitute for DIT in appropriate clinical scenarios."
}

