  "summary": "The 2017 McDonald criteria for MS diagnosis require demonstration of dissemination in space (DIS) and dissemination in time (DIT). DIS requires lesions in at least 2 of 4 characteristic CNS regions. DIT can be demonstrated by new lesions on follow-up MRI, simultaneous enhancing and non-enhancing lesions, or CSF-specific oligoclonal bands (new in 2017 revision). Importantly, the 2017 criteria allow CSF oligoclonal bands to substitute for DIT even in the absence of follow-up MRI evidence, which was a major change from the 2010 revision."
