      "key_finding": "VP shunt improves the NPH gait component; the spastic myelopathy component persists. Combined outcomes are better than either condition alone untreated."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Published literature notes that NPH and cervical myelopathy may coexist and produce overlapping symptoms (gait disorder, bladder dysfunction). Key distinguishing features include gait quality (magnetic/wide-based in NPH versus spastic/narrow-based in myelopathy), imaging criteria for each condition, and response to tap trial or drainage. VP shunt outcomes in patients with concurrent spinal disease show improvement in the NPH gait component while the myelopathy component may persist. Clinical correlation required to determine applicability in individual cases."
}

