      "key_finding": "Anti-Hu (ANNA-1) is associated with SCLC in >80% of cases. Paraneoplastic limbic encephalitis with anti-Hu has poor prognosis compared to anti-LGI1/NMDAR because Hu targets intracellular antigens causing direct neuronal destruction. Tumor treatment (SCLC chemotherapy) is the primary treatment \u2014 immunotherapy alone has limited efficacy. NCSE in paraneoplastic encephalitis responds to AEDs + immunotherapy but neurological improvement is modest."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Anti-Hu (ANNA-1) antibody-associated paraneoplastic neurological syndrome is most frequently associated with small cell lung carcinoma (approximately 75-80% of cases) and other neuroendocrine tumors. The Hu antigen is intracellular, which is associated with a lower rate of neurological improvement with immunotherapy compared to antibodies targeting cell-surface antigens. Tumor-directed therapy is the primary management approach in published case series. Limbic encephalitis is the most common neurological phenotype; seizures and EEG abnormalities including LPDs and NCSE have been reported. Prognosis is generally guarded; outcome is correlated with tumor response to therapy."
}

